@model Korisnik

@* The predavač's kontakt podaci, set apart because they are what an učenik came for. There
   is no messaging on the platform — this is the handoff from the application to the čas, and
   both are clickable so a phone dials and a mail client opens.

   A partial because three screens show it: the oglas detail page, the profil predavača,
   and the omiljeni list. They are the same handoff and must not drift into being spelled
   three ways, which is the argument PrikazOcene already makes about the ocena line beside it.

   The model is nullable for the reason KontaktPodaci's own doc gives: Oglas.Predavac is a
   nullable navigation, the value is never actually absent, and a guard against a state the
   application cannot produce would be dead code.

   The heading is an h2 on both callers: on the profil it follows the h1 that names the
   predavač, and on the oglas page it is the sibling of that card's own "Predavač". An h3
   would read better under the latter and skip a level under the former. *@

<div class="border rounded p-3 bg-light">
    <h2 class="h6 mb-2">Kontakt podaci</h2>

    <dl class="row mb-0 small">
        <dt class="col-4 fw-normal text-muted">Email</dt>
        <dd class="col-8 mb-1 text-break">
            <a href="@KontaktPodaci.EmailHref(Model?.Email)">@Model?.Email</a>
        </dd>

        <dt class="col-4 fw-normal text-muted">Telefon</dt>
        <dd class="col-8 mb-0 text-break">
            <a href="@KontaktPodaci.TelefonHref(Model?.Telefon)">@Model?.Telefon</a>
        </dd>
    </dl>

    <div class="form-text mt-2 mb-0">
        Čas dogovarate direktno sa predavačem — platforma ne zakazuje termine.
    </div>
</div>
